<title>USA: Tele-Comms to merge phone services - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Tele-Comms to merge phone services - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The telephone service operations of Tele-Communications Inc will be merged into a single unit, The Wall Street Journal reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>It is the latest in a series of restructuring moves by the nation's largest cable operator amid poorly performing stock, $14.5 billion in debt and diminished profit margins, the story says.</p>
</text>
